# RBAC & Multi-Tenancy Rules

- Roles: `SUPER_ADMIN`, `COMPANY_OWNER`, `DEPARTMENT_HEAD`, `TEAM_LEAD`, `EMPLOYEE`.
  Single source of truth for permissions: `lib/rbac/role-matrix.ts`.
- Every gated UI element wraps in `<Can action="..." resource="...">` — never an inline
  `if (role === 'COMPANY_OWNER')` scattered through JSX. If a new permission check is
  needed, add it to `role-matrix.ts` first.
- `middleware.ts` validates on every request: (a) session exists, (b) for company-scoped
  routes, the `[companySlug]` param matches the session's `company_id`, (c) for
  super-admin routes, role is `SUPER_ADMIN`. A 403 page, not a redirect loop, on failure.
- Never rely on hiding a nav item as the only protection for a route — every route under
  `(platform-admin)` and role-restricted sub-routes under `(company)` must also be
  server-guarded (page-level session check or middleware matcher).
- API calls never take `company_id`/`department_id`/`team_id` from client-controlled state
  as the sole authorization signal — they're passed for *filtering* convenience only; the
  server re-derives allowed scope from the session token.

Role dashboards and capability matrix: skill `intelliroi-architecture` and
`.cursor/skills/03-ROLE-HIERARCHY-AND-DASHBOARDS.md`.
